    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are a few options for a polite and professional rejection email. You want to acknowledge their effort, which is key, and then deliver the news gently. Remember to keep the tone appreciative, even though it's a rejection.\n\nHere is a draft you can adapt:\n\n\"Dear [Candidate Name],\n\nThank you so much for taking the time to interview with us and for making it to the final round for the [Job Title] position. We truly enjoyed learning more about your experience and skills during the interview process. We have decided to move forward with another candidate whose background was a slightly closer match to our immediate needs for this specific role. We sincerely appreciate your interest in [Company Name] and wish you the very best in your job search.\"\n\n**Why this works:** It's direct but warm, validates their hard work, and provides a gentle reason without going into unnecessary detail. It keeps the door open for future opportunities, which is always good practice.",
